{"sourceSha256": "9082ae1c2062667a09f3a8d93ff79176bef1d3a5bb45c9208db471768071a98b", "text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\n\nWRITING SUB-TEST: MEDICINE\n\nTIME ALLOWED:\n\nREADING TIME: 5 MINUTES\nWRITING TIME: 40 MINUTES\n\nRead the case notes below and complete the writing task which follows.\n\nPatient History\nDOB\nPMH\n\nTracy Bowen (Ms)\n22/7/88\n\nChildhood asthma - worse with dust, exercise, smoke, cat hair, change in temperature.\n\nRecurrent bronchitis.\nFather heavy smoker ~ house smoky.\nSalbutamo! inhaler, beclomethasone prn\n\nIrregular menstrual periods since menarche. Very infrequent, up to 90-day\nintermenstrual interval. Frequently with dysmenorrhoea. Stress related to parents’\ndivorce (2002). Adolescent acne since 3/12 (‘pus-filled’).\n\nAbdominal exam - NAD\n\nRectal exam - NAD\n\nFHx — no genetic anomalies\n\nBreast development normal\n\nIdiopathic oligomenorrhoea, primary dysmenorrhoea\n\nOral contraceptive pill (Diane-35, 2mg — low dose)\nAnalgesia (naproxen)\nReassurance\n\nAcne - facial + upper back, shoulders and neck.\n\nOE: deep, inflamed nodules and pus-filled cysts with scarring on face, neck,\nupper back and shoulders.\n\nDeep acne\n\nAntibiotic therapy: tetracycline 250mg qid; tetracycline ointment 1% 5g, apply\nliberally bd\n\nAcne - unchanged. Cyst-like, leaves scars. C/o diarrhoea, vaginal candidiasis and\nsore tongue since 4/52.\n\nCystic acne\n\nRefer to dermatologist for Roaccutane (isotretinoin) capsules 30mg bd. Isotrex gel\n\n0.05% - apply at night.\nRW 2/52.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\n\nWRITING SUB-TEST: MEDICINE\n\nTIME ALLOWED:\n\nREADING TIME: 5 MINUTES\nWRITING TIME: 40 MINUTES\n\nRead the case notes below and complete the writing task which follows.\n\nPatient History\nDOB\nPMH\n\nTracy Bowen (Ms)\n22/7/88\n\nChildhood asthma - worse with dust, exercise, smoke, cat hair, change in temperature.\n\nRecurrent bronchitis.\nFather heavy smoker ~ house smoky.\nSalbutamo! inhaler, beclomethasone prn\n\nIrregular menstrual periods since menarche. Very infrequent, up to 90-day\nintermenstrual interval. Frequently with dysmenorrhoea. Stress related to parents’\ndivorce (2002). Adolescent acne since 3/12 (‘pus-filled’).\n\nAbdominal exam - NAD\n\nRectal exam - NAD\n\nFHx — no genetic anomalies\n\nBreast development normal\n\nIdiopathic oligomenorrhoea, primary dysmenorrhoea\n\nOral contraceptive pill (Diane-35, 2mg — low dose)\nAnalgesia (naproxen)\nReassurance\n\nAcne - facial + upper back, shoulders and neck.\n\nOE: deep, inflamed nodules and pus-filled cysts with scarring on face, neck,\nupper back and shoulders.\n\nDeep acne\n\nAntibiotic therapy: tetracycline 250mg qid; tetracycline ointment 1% 5g, apply\nliberally bd\n\nAcne - unchanged. Cyst-like, leaves scars. C/o diarrhoea, vaginal candidiasis and\nsore tongue since 4/52.\n\nCystic acne\n\nRefer to dermatologist for Roaccutane (isotretinoin) capsules 30mg bd. Isotrex gel\n\n0.05% - apply at night.\nRW 2/52.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2144.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST", "lines": [{"text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST", "x": 0.02146, "y": 0.00643, "width": 0.65112, "height": 0.02821, "confidence": 0.961, "words": [{"text": "OCCUPATIONAL", "x": 0.02146, "width": 0.33302, "confidence": 0.964}, {"text": "ENGLISH", "x": 0.36847, "width": 0.1833, "confidence": 0.959}, {"text": "TEST", "x": 0.56576, "width": 0.10681, "confidence": 0.962}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "WRITING SUB-TEST: MEDICINE", "lines": [{"text": "WRITING SUB-TEST: MEDICINE", "x": 0.02052, "y": 0.0625, "width": 0.39879, "height": 0.01714, "confidence": 0.925, "words": [{"text": "WRITING", "x": 0.02052, "width": 0.10728, "confidence": 0.931}, {"text": "SUB-TEST:", "x": 0.13573, "width": 0.12733, "confidence": 0.886}, {"text": "MEDICINE", "x": 0.29711, "width": 0.1222, "confidence": 0.96}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "TIME ALLOWED:", "lines": [{"text": "TIME ALL